      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello. What brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S020",
      "patient_response": "Well... I came in because I keep hearing these voices. They are as clear as somebody standing right there in my little studio, just saying my name and telling me my work is being judged. And I don't know why they'd say that, because I work real hard. I'm a personal care aide, you know? I take care of folks who can't do for themselves. Just yesterday I was over at Mr. Miller's place, helping him with his meals. He likes his soup piping hot, burns his tongue half the time, but he won't eat it if it's even a little cold. I always have to use that old microwave of his that smells like burnt popcorn. I told his daughter she needs to buy him a new one, but she never listens to me. But... yeah, even when I go home and my house is completely quiet, and nobody is there with me... I still hear them. Just judging my work.",
