    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "About how long have you been hearing these voices?",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "It's been... I'd say about nine months now. Nine months of the voices, and just this... this constant, fixed fear I have that my work is being watched all the time. \n\nI know it was nine months ago because it started right around the time I bought my new work shoes. They're these thick, white non-slip ones. You really gotta have good shoes when you're lifting folks, plus the linoleum floors over at Mrs. Gable's house—she's another client of mine—they get so slippery if you spill even a drop of water. It's like an ice rink in her kitchen. My cousin slipped at her job at the grocery store and messed up her knee so bad she was stuck on the couch for a whole year. She just sat there watching those daytime judge shows, eating those little square orange cheese crackers. I can't stand those crackers, they get all gummy in your teeth and turn your fingers completely orange, like you painted them. \n\nBut I couldn't just sit around like her, you know? I have to keep working, I have bills. I'm a hard worker. But... yeah, nine months of them watching me and saying those things.",
