    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "During these past nine months, have you experienced periods of feeling deeply down, depressed, or losing interest in things you usually enjoy?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "Depressed? No, I wouldn't say that. I don't really get down like that, I don't have the time to sit around moping. I still like doing my usual things. Like my knitting... I knit these little square blankets for the premature babies down at the hospital. You have to use the softest yarn, 100% acrylic, because you can't use wool on those little babies. \n\nWool makes me itch so bad anyway. I bought this wool sweater at a thrift store a few years back, a really pretty blue one, kind of like a robin's egg? But I wore it to church and I was scratching my neck the entire sermon. Reverend Thomas kept looking right at me from the pulpit, he probably thought I had a rash or fleas or something. He always gives these really long sermons, mostly from the Old Testament. I don't know why he likes it so much, it's just a bunch of rules about what you can and can't eat. I love a good pork chop, so I just tune that part out. You gotta fry them in a cast iron skillet with a little bit of bacon grease to get that good crust on the outside. If you use a regular non-stick pan, they just get gray and rubbery. \n\nBut no, I haven't been sad or lost interest in anything. Just... just hearing them judge me.",
