    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Do you use any recreational drugs, or drink alcohol?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, I don't touch any of that stuff. Drugs and alcohol, they just mess with your head and your body. I've seen it enough with some of the folks in my neighborhood. There's this one man, Mr. Henderson, lives a few doors down from me. He sits on his porch all day drinking those tall cans of beer in the brown paper bags. He leaves the empty cans all over his front lawn, and when the wind picks up, they blow right into my flower beds. I have these beautiful petunias I planted in the spring. You have to water them every single morning before the sun gets too hot, otherwise the leaves get all crispy and brown. I use this little green watering can I got at the hardware store. It has a little spout that sprinkles the water real gentle, like rain. If you use a hose, it just blasts the dirt right out of the pot and makes a huge muddy mess on the sidewalk. And then you track it into the house... and I tell you, getting mud out of a white rug is impossible. I tried that foam spray stuff once, but it just left a big yellow stain that looked worse than the mud. So I had to put a coffee table over it to hide it. It's a nice table, though, real oak. Heavy as a car. But no, I don't drink or do drugs. Never have.",
